# ============================================================
# JuRu — start here
#
# This folder (examples/guide/) teaches the whole language in
# 14 small, runnable lessons — one keyword at a time.
#
# Run this file:
#     python3 juru.py examples/guide/00_start_here.jr
# ...then move on to 01_say.jr, 02_if_else.jr, and so on.
#
# This first lesson is not about one keyword yet — it is about
# the two ideas every program is built from:
#   1. a value gets a name   (a variable)
#   2. the computer shows it (say)
# ============================================================

# 1. A variable: a name that holds a value.
#    No type to write, no ceremony — just name = value.
name = "Ada"
age = 12

# 2. Text joins text with +.
say("Hello, " + name + "!")

# 3. Text joins a number with + too — JuRu converts it for you.
say("You are " + age + " years old.")

# 4. Math just works: whole numbers, decimals, the usual rules.
say(2 + 3)
say(10 / 4)

# 5. A variable can change later — it is just a name.
age = age + 1
say("Next year: " + age)

# That is the whole ramp. Every lesson from here teaches one
# keyword of the language — 19 keywords in total, that is the
# complete list, and the guide covers every single one.
